  data: {
    LLM: "For Beginners:\n1. Remember the two cards you viewed at the start\n2. Replace high cards (10s, 9s, 8s) with lower cards\n3. Kings (0 points) are valuable - keep them\n4. Don't knock unless you think you have the lowest score\n\n1. Track which cards have been discarded to know what's available\n2. Consider the risk of drawing vs taking a known discard\n3. In 6-card, watch which cards opponents are turning face up\n4. Try to create pairs in columns for zero scoring\n\n1. Calculate probabilities of drawing useful cards\n2. Bluff by knocking with a higher score to pressure opponents\n3. Memorize all visible cards to deduce opponent holdings\n4. Endgame calculation when few cards remain in stock",
